# p_6d9a — Journal Left at the Bedroom Desk, Not Taken to Work

p_b7c2 claims Marco's journal is out of the house during his 14:00–22:00 shift, but the claim was contradicted twice (journal sighted in the house) and 3 looks at the nightstand found it absent. The journal is a home object: Marco journals in the early morning (around 6:00–8:00) as part of his pre-work routine, then leaves it at the bedroom desk (desk_b1) before heading out. It does not travel with him. The per-object evidence places it mostly at the nightstand, but the 3 empty looks at the nightstand during work hours suggest it has been moved to the desk after a morning journaling session. In the evening, when Marco returns around 23:00, he may move it back to the nightstand for the next morning.

This document differs from p_b7c2 (journal out of house 14–22h) by keeping the journal in the house at the bedroom desk. It would be refuted if the journal is sighted out of the house on a weekday afternoon, or if it is consistently at the nightstand (not the desk) during 14:00–22:00.

